{"parentUuid":"2d46ac1f-ce1a-425d-94ce-004107680b8f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a8eb74f4-7d35-4d51-ba40-5a7449d2743d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GEMTRirskAsXLrZn5fsZyT","type":"tool_result","content":"=================== guides/analytics.md\n# Analytics\n\n> Cross-platform metrics for every post you publish — and every post you didn't.\n\nPlugKit collects metrics in the background and serves them from its own store.\nThat means one request answers for **every connected account at once**, over any\nwindow, sorted however you like — instead of one call per account per platform,\neach with a different shape.\n\nIt also means the numbers have an age. Every response carries `lastSyncAt` and\n`nextSyncAt` so you can show it; see [How collection\nworks](/concepts/analytics-collection) for the cadence.\n\n<Note>\n  Analytics are included on every plan and every account, from the trial\n  onwards. Nothing here is gated.\n</Note>\n\n## Summary\n\nThe headline numbers over a window, each with its change against the previous\nperiod of the same length:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/summary?from=2026-07-24\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"window\": { \"from\": \"2026-07-24T…\", \"to\": \"2026-08-23T…\", \"maxHistoryDays\": 90, \"clamped\": false },\n  \"posts\": { \"value\": 194, \"change\": 54.0 },\n  \"engagementRate\": { \"value\": 6.8, \"change\": 0.5 },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"reach\":       { \"value\": 662700, \"change\": 64.0 },\n    \"likes\":       { \"value\": 23100,  \"change\": 15.4 },\n    \"impressions\": { \"value\": 1310000, \"change\": 29.4 },\n    \"clicks\":      { \"value\": null,   \"change\": null }\n  },\n  \"followers\": { \"total\": 726600, \"change\": 1970 },\n  \"bestPost\": { \"id\": \"sp_…\", \"platform\": \"instagram\", \"engagement\": 4120, \"permalink\": \"https://…\" },\n  \"lastSyncAt\": \"2026-08-23T14:31:00.000Z\",\n  \"nextSyncAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:19:00.000Z\"\n}\n```\n\n<Warning>\n  `null` is not zero. A `null` metric means the platform doesn't expose it for\n  that account — TikTok has no reach, YouTube has no impressions. Rendering it\n  as `0` skews every average you compute downstream.\n</Warning>\n\nChanges follow the unit of what they measure: a **volume** changes in percent,\na **rate** changes in points. `engagementRate.change: 0.5` means half a point\n(6.3% → 6.8%), not half a percent.\n\n## Posts\n\nEvery post with its metrics, sorted by whichever one matters:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/posts?sortBy=engagement&limit=10\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n| Parameter | Values |\n| - | - |\n| `platform` | `instagram`, `facebook`, `tiktok`, `youtube`, `x` |\n| `profileId` / `accountId` | Narrow to one profile or one account |\n| `source` | `all` (default), `plugkit`, `external` |\n| `from` / `to` | ISO dates. Defaults to the last 30 days |\n| `sortBy` | `date`, `engagement`, `likes`, `comments`, `shares`, `saves`, `views`, `impressions`, `reach`, `clicks` |\n| `order` | `asc`, `desc` (default) |\n| `page` / `limit` | Up to 100 per page |\n\n### Posts you didn't publish through PlugKit\n\nThe collector mirrors what each platform lists, so a post published straight\nfrom the Instagram app shows up here too, marked `source: \"external\"`. That's\nwhat makes the numbers match the platform's own dashboard on day one, instead\nof only counting what has gone through the API since you connected.\n\nUse `source=plugkit` when you specifically want to measure your own automation.\n\n## Over time\n\nOne metric, bucketed by day, week or month, optionally split by platform — the\nshape a stacked chart wants:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/timeseries?metric=likes&granularity=week&byPlatform=true\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"metric\": \"likes\",\n  \"granularity\": \"week\",\n  \"series\": [\n    { \"date\": \"2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z\", \"platform\": \"instagram\", \"total\": 5200 },\n    { \"date\": \"2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z\", \"platform\": \"tiktok\",    \"total\": 2400 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nPosts are grouped by **publication date**, and their current metrics summed:\n\"likes for the week of the 3rd\" means \"likes earned by the posts published that\nweek\". That's the reading that tells you what to publish next.\n\n## Platform breakdown\n\nOne row per network over the window — posts, every metric, and the engagement\nrate:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/platforms\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n## Best time to post\n\nAverage engagement per weekday and hour, read in the timezone you ask for:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/best-times?timezone=Europe/Paris\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"timezone\": \"Europe/Paris\",\n  \"cells\": [\n    { \"weekday\": 4, \"hour\": 20, \"posts\": 7, \"averageEngagement\": 1580 },\n    { \"weekday\": 6, \"hour\": 3,  \"posts\": 1, \"averageEngagement\": 4200 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`weekday` is `0` for Sunday, following Postgres. **Always pass a timezone** — an\nhour-of-day grid read in UTC is off by your users' whole offset, and it fails\nsilently, because every cell still has a plausible number in it.\n\nCheck `posts` before acting on a cell. The second row above has the best average\nof the set and is worth nothing: one post is a coincidence, not a slot.\n\n## Engagement accumulation\n\nHow fast a post earns its final engagement, by age bucket — the answer to \"is it\nstill worth watching, or is it done?\":\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/accumulation\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"buckets\": [\n    { \"bucket\": \"6h\",  \"samples\": 40, \"share\": 48.9 },\n    { \"bucket\": \"24h\", \"samples\": 36, \"share\": 76.5 },\n    { \"bucket\": \"7d\",  \"samples\": 25, \"share\": 94.0 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`share` is the percentage of final engagement already earned at that age,\naveraged over the posts in the window. It fills in as your posts age — a brand\nnew account only has the early buckets.\n\n## Followers\n\nFollower count over time, per account, with growth:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/followers?granularity=day\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n<Note>\n  The series starts the day the account was connected. No platform hands back\n  the follower history it didn't record — it can only be measured forward, one\n  day at a time. Connect early.\n</Note>\n\n## Refresh on demand\n\nSomeone just published from the platform's own app and wants to see it now:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl -X POST https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/sync \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{ \"accountId\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\" }'\n```\n\nWith an `accountId`, the platform is queried within the request. Without one,\nevery account of the caller is moved to the front of the queue and picked up on\nthe next cycle.\n\nCalls within 15 seconds of each other on the same account are ignored — a\ndashboard that refreshes on focus can't turn into a burst of platform calls.\n\n## Live reads\n\nThe endpoints above never touch a platform. When you want the value *right now*\nfor one object — and are willing to pay for it on metered platforms — two\npass-through reads remain:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/accounts/ACCOUNT_ID/analytics -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/accounts/ACCOUNT_ID/media/MEDIA_ID/analytics -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\nThey return one object, no history and no comparison, and each one is billed on\nX. Prefer `/v1/analytics/*` for anything you'd put in a dashboard.\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"How collection works\" icon=\"rotate\" href=\"/concepts/analytics-collection\">\n    Cadences, freshness, history depth, and what each platform actually exposes.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Try it live\" icon=\"code\" href=\"/api-reference\">\n    Every analytics endpoint in the playground.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\n\n=================== guides/webhooks.md\n# Webhooks\n\n> Get told when a post goes live, a message arrives, or an account drops.\n\nRegister an HTTPS endpoint and PlugKit posts an event to it when something\nhappens — no polling.\n\n## Create an endpoint\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl -X POST https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"url\": \"https://your-app.com/hooks/plugkit\",\n    \"events\": [\"post.published\", \"message.received\"]\n  }'\n```\n\nOmit `events` (or send an empty list) to receive everything, including events\nadded later.\n\n<Warning>\n  The response contains the signing secret (`whsec_…`) **once**. Store it now —\n  it is never shown again, and you need it to verify deliveries.\n</Warning>\n\n## Events\n\n| Event | Fired when |\n| - | - |\n| `post.published` | The post is live on every one of its targets. |\n| `post.partial` | Some targets published, others failed. |\n| `post.failed` | No target published. |\n| `message.received` | An inbound message landed in the inbox. |\n| `comment.received` | A comment arrived on one of the account's posts. |\n| `comment.dm_sent` | A [comment → DM automation](/guides/campaigns) sent its private message. |\n| `broadcast.finished` | A broadcast finished serving every recipient. |\n| `account.disconnected` | An account was disconnected, or its token died. |\n| `usage.threshold_reached` | Pay-per-call spend passed 80% of the monthly cap — once a month, before anything pauses. |\n\nThe list is closed and names are `object.past_tense`. New events are added over\ntime; existing ones are never renamed.\n\n## Payload\n\nEvery delivery shares one envelope:\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"id\": \"evt_9f2c…\",\n  \"type\": \"post.published\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T14:31:02.184Z\",\n  \"data\": { }\n}\n```\n\n`data` carries the resource in the same shape the REST API returns it, so the\npost in `post.published` is the post you'd get from `GET /v1/posts/{id}`.\n\n## Verifying a delivery\n\nEach request carries an `x-plugkit-signature` header:\n\n```\nx-plugkit-signature: t=1756045862,v1=6f3b…\n```\n\n`v1` is the HMAC-SHA256 of `<t>.<raw body>`, keyed with your endpoint secret.\nCompute it over the **raw** body — parsing and re-serialising the JSON changes\nthe bytes and breaks the comparison.\n\n<CodeGroup>\n  ```ts TypeScript theme={null}\n  import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from \"crypto\";\n\n  function verify(rawBody: string, header: string, secret: string): boolean {\n    const parts = Object.fromEntries(\n      header.split(\",\").map((kv) => kv.split(\"=\") as [string, string]),\n    );\n    const expected = createHmac(\"sha256\", secret)\n      .update(`${parts.t}.${rawBody}`)\n      .digest(\"hex\");\n\n    // Reject anything older than five minutes to blunt replays.\n    if (Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number(parts.t)) > 300) return false;\n\n    return timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(expected), Buffer.from(parts.v1));\n  }\n  ```\n\n  ```python Python theme={null}\n  import hmac, hashlib, time\n\n  def verify(raw_body: bytes, header: str, secret: str) -> bool:\n      parts = dict(kv.split(\"=\", 1) for kv in header.split(\",\"))\n      expected = hmac.new(\n          secret.encode(), f\"{parts['t']}.\".encode() + raw_body, hashlib.sha256\n      ).hexdigest()\n      if abs(time.time() - int(parts[\"t\"])) > 300:\n          return False\n      return hmac.compare_digest(expected, parts[\"v1\"])\n  ```\n</CodeGroup>\n\n## Delivery and retries\n\nAnswer `2xx` within **10 seconds**. Anything else — an error status, a timeout,\na connection refused — is retried up to **6 attempts** with backoff: 30s, 2min,\n8min, 32min, \\~2h, then the delivery is marked `FAILED`.\n\nEvents are queued and sent by a worker, never inside the request that triggered\nthem. A slow endpoint of yours never slows down a publication, and a broken one\nnever makes it fail.\n\nDeliveries are **at least once**: a retry after a response you sent late will\narrive twice. Deduplicate on the payload's `id`.\n\nInspect what happened:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID/deliveries \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\nEach row carries the event, the attempt count, the response status and the last\nerror.\n\n## Managing endpoints\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n\ncurl -X PATCH https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{ \"enabled\": false }'\n\ncurl -X DELETE https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n<Note>\n  These are PlugKit's **outbound** webhooks. The inbound plumbing — subscribing\n  an account to Meta's own webhooks so DMs reach the inbox at all — happens\n  automatically when an account is connected. It can be re-run for Instagram\n  (`POST /v1/connect/instagram/{accountId}/subscribe-webhooks`) and WhatsApp\n  (`POST /v1/connect/whatsapp/{accountId}/subscribe-webhooks`); a Facebook Page\n  subscribes once at connection time, so a Page that missed it has to be\n  reconnected.\n</Note>\n\n\n=================== mcp/overview.md\n# MCP server\n\n> Give Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, VS Code or any MCP client the ability to publish, read and reply on your social accounts.\n\nPlugKit ships a hosted **MCP server**: the same capabilities as the REST API,\nexposed as tools an AI assistant can call. Point a client at one URL, sign in,\nand the assistant can list your connected accounts, publish a post, triage the\ninbox, or pull analytics — no code, no SDK.\n\n```\nhttps://api.plugkit.co/mcp\n```\n\n<Note>\n  Transport is **Streamable HTTP** (stateless). There is nothing to install and\n  nothing to run locally — no `npx`, no local proxy.\n</Note>\n\n## Connect in one click\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"Claude\" icon=\"message\" href=\"/mcp/clients#claude-web-desktop-mobile\">\n    Customize → Connectors → Add → Custom connector → paste the URL.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"ChatGPT\" icon=\"sparkles\" href=\"/mcp/clients#chatgpt\">\n    Developer mode → chatgpt.com/plugins → **+** → paste the URL.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Claude Code\" icon=\"terminal\" href=\"/mcp/clients#claude-code\">\n    `claude mcp add -t http plugkit https://api.plugkit.co/mcp`\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Cursor\" icon=\"arrow-pointer\" href=\"/mcp/clients#cursor\">\n    One-click install link, or three lines in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"VS Code\" icon=\"code\" href=\"/mcp/clients#vs-code\">\n    One-click install link, or `code --add-mcp`.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\nFastest path of all: **[Assistants & API keys](https://plugkit.co/dashboard/mcp)**\nin the dashboard walks through one client at a time, with an install button or\nthe exact values to paste — and then confirms when the server has actually seen\nyour assistant connect.\n\n## Authentication\n\nTwo ways in, same account scoping as the REST API — an assistant only ever sees\nthe profiles, accounts, posts and conversations of the PlugKit user it acts for.\n\n<Tabs>\n  <Tab title=\"Sign in (OAuth)\">\n    The recommended path, and the only one that needs no secret in a config file.\n    PlugKit is a full OAuth 2.1 authorization server (PKCE, no client secret): the\n    client sends you to a PlugKit consent screen, you approve, and it stores a\n    token of its own.\n\n    You choose what you grant:\n\n    | Scope | What the assistant can do |\n    | - | - |\n    | `mcp:read` | Read profiles, accounts, posts, conversations and analytics. Write tools are not even listed. |\n    | `mcp:write` | Everything above, plus publish, send messages, reply to comments, connect and disconnect accounts. |\n\n    Revoke any assistant at any time from **Settings → Connected apps** in the\n    dashboard.\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"API key\">\n    For clients without OAuth support, send a key as a plain Bearer header:\n\n    ```json theme={null}\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"plugkit\": {\n          \"type\": \"http\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.plugkit.co/mcp\",\n          \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_your_key\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n\n    Create the key in the dashboard's [API Keys](https://plugkit.co/dashboard/api-keys)\n    section. A key carries **full access** — it has no scopes — so prefer OAuth\n    when the client supports it.\n  </Tab>\n</Tabs>\n\n## What an assistant can do\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"Publish\" icon=\"paper-plane\">\n    Draft, schedule and publish to several accounts at once, with media.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Inbox\" icon=\"inbox\">\n    Read and answer Instagram, WhatsApp and Telegram conversations.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Comments\" icon=\"comments\">\n    Read comments on a published post and reply publicly.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Analytics\" icon=\"chart-line\">\n    Ranked posts, trends, follower growth and best posting times — read from the\n    collected store, so one call covers every account.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Campaigns & ads\" icon=\"bullhorn\">\n    Comment → DM automations, broadcasts, follow-up sequences, and Meta ad\n    campaigns.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Connections\" icon=\"plug\">\n    Hand the user an OAuth link to connect a new account, or disconnect one.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"All 103 tools\" icon=\"wrench\" href=\"/mcp/tools\">\n    The full reference, plus the three ready-made workflows.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\n## Safety\n\nPublishing a post, sending a message and replying to a comment are **public and\nimmediate**. The server instructs the model to show the exact content and get\nyour approval before calling those tools, but that is a prompt, not a lock — the\nreal guarantees are the ones you control:\n\n* Grant `mcp:read` only, when you just want reporting and triage.\n* Review the accounts a connected assistant can reach with `whoami`.\n* Revoke from **Settings → Connected apps** the moment you're done.\n\n<Warning>\n  `delete_profile` cascades to its accounts, posts and conversations, and\n  `revoke_api_key` can revoke the very key the connection runs on. Both are\n  write-scope tools — another reason to hand out `mcp:read` by default.\n</Warning>\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a27fa7c8-9f7f-497a-bbfd-65aaedd54b08","timestamp":"2026-10-03T08:51:11.917Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=================== guides/analytics.md\n# Analytics\n\n> Cross-platform metrics for every post you publish — and every post you didn't.\n\nPlugKit collects metrics in the background and serves them from its own store.\nThat means one request answers for **every connected account at once**, over any\nwindow, sorted however you like — instead of one call per account per platform,\neach with a different shape.\n\nIt also means the numbers have an age. Every response carries `lastSyncAt` and\n`nextSyncAt` so you can show it; see [How collection\nworks](/concepts/analytics-collection) for the cadence.\n\n<Note>\n  Analytics are included on every plan and every account, from the trial\n  onwards. Nothing here is gated.\n</Note>\n\n## Summary\n\nThe headline numbers over a window, each with its change against the previous\nperiod of the same length:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/summary?from=2026-07-24\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"window\": { \"from\": \"2026-07-24T…\", \"to\": \"2026-08-23T…\", \"maxHistoryDays\": 90, \"clamped\": false },\n  \"posts\": { \"value\": 194, \"change\": 54.0 },\n  \"engagementRate\": { \"value\": 6.8, \"change\": 0.5 },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"reach\":       { \"value\": 662700, \"change\": 64.0 },\n    \"likes\":       { \"value\": 23100,  \"change\": 15.4 },\n    \"impressions\": { \"value\": 1310000, \"change\": 29.4 },\n    \"clicks\":      { \"value\": null,   \"change\": null }\n  },\n  \"followers\": { \"total\": 726600, \"change\": 1970 },\n  \"bestPost\": { \"id\": \"sp_…\", \"platform\": \"instagram\", \"engagement\": 4120, \"permalink\": \"https://…\" },\n  \"lastSyncAt\": \"2026-08-23T14:31:00.000Z\",\n  \"nextSyncAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:19:00.000Z\"\n}\n```\n\n<Warning>\n  `null` is not zero. A `null` metric means the platform doesn't expose it for\n  that account — TikTok has no reach, YouTube has no impressions. Rendering it\n  as `0` skews every average you compute downstream.\n</Warning>\n\nChanges follow the unit of what they measure: a **volume** changes in percent,\na **rate** changes in points. `engagementRate.change: 0.5` means half a point\n(6.3% → 6.8%), not half a percent.\n\n## Posts\n\nEvery post with its metrics, sorted by whichever one matters:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/posts?sortBy=engagement&limit=10\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n| Parameter | Values |\n| - | - |\n| `platform` | `instagram`, `facebook`, `tiktok`, `youtube`, `x` |\n| `profileId` / `accountId` | Narrow to one profile or one account |\n| `source` | `all` (default), `plugkit`, `external` |\n| `from` / `to` | ISO dates. Defaults to the last 30 days |\n| `sortBy` | `date`, `engagement`, `likes`, `comments`, `shares`, `saves`, `views`, `impressions`, `reach`, `clicks` |\n| `order` | `asc`, `desc` (default) |\n| `page` / `limit` | Up to 100 per page |\n\n### Posts you didn't publish through PlugKit\n\nThe collector mirrors what each platform lists, so a post published straight\nfrom the Instagram app shows up here too, marked `source: \"external\"`. That's\nwhat makes the numbers match the platform's own dashboard on day one, instead\nof only counting what has gone through the API since you connected.\n\nUse `source=plugkit` when you specifically want to measure your own automation.\n\n## Over time\n\nOne metric, bucketed by day, week or month, optionally split by platform — the\nshape a stacked chart wants:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/timeseries?metric=likes&granularity=week&byPlatform=true\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"metric\": \"likes\",\n  \"granularity\": \"week\",\n  \"series\": [\n    { \"date\": \"2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z\", \"platform\": \"instagram\", \"total\": 5200 },\n    { \"date\": \"2026-08-03T00:00:00.000Z\", \"platform\": \"tiktok\",    \"total\": 2400 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nPosts are grouped by **publication date**, and their current metrics summed:\n\"likes for the week of the 3rd\" means \"likes earned by the posts published that\nweek\". That's the reading that tells you what to publish next.\n\n## Platform breakdown\n\nOne row per network over the window — posts, every metric, and the engagement\nrate:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/platforms\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n## Best time to post\n\nAverage engagement per weekday and hour, read in the timezone you ask for:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/best-times?timezone=Europe/Paris\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"timezone\": \"Europe/Paris\",\n  \"cells\": [\n    { \"weekday\": 4, \"hour\": 20, \"posts\": 7, \"averageEngagement\": 1580 },\n    { \"weekday\": 6, \"hour\": 3,  \"posts\": 1, \"averageEngagement\": 4200 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`weekday` is `0` for Sunday, following Postgres. **Always pass a timezone** — an\nhour-of-day grid read in UTC is off by your users' whole offset, and it fails\nsilently, because every cell still has a plausible number in it.\n\nCheck `posts` before acting on a cell. The second row above has the best average\nof the set and is worth nothing: one post is a coincidence, not a slot.\n\n## Engagement accumulation\n\nHow fast a post earns its final engagement, by age bucket — the answer to \"is it\nstill worth watching, or is it done?\":\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/accumulation\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n```json Response (trimmed) theme={null}\n{\n  \"buckets\": [\n    { \"bucket\": \"6h\",  \"samples\": 40, \"share\": 48.9 },\n    { \"bucket\": \"24h\", \"samples\": 36, \"share\": 76.5 },\n    { \"bucket\": \"7d\",  \"samples\": 25, \"share\": 94.0 }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`share` is the percentage of final engagement already earned at that age,\naveraged over the posts in the window. It fills in as your posts age — a brand\nnew account only has the early buckets.\n\n## Followers\n\nFollower count over time, per account, with growth:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl \"https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/followers?granularity=day\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n<Note>\n  The series starts the day the account was connected. No platform hands back\n  the follower history it didn't record — it can only be measured forward, one\n  day at a time. Connect early.\n</Note>\n\n## Refresh on demand\n\nSomeone just published from the platform's own app and wants to see it now:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl -X POST https://api.plugkit.co/v1/analytics/sync \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{ \"accountId\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\" }'\n```\n\nWith an `accountId`, the platform is queried within the request. Without one,\nevery account of the caller is moved to the front of the queue and picked up on\nthe next cycle.\n\nCalls within 15 seconds of each other on the same account are ignored — a\ndashboard that refreshes on focus can't turn into a burst of platform calls.\n\n## Live reads\n\nThe endpoints above never touch a platform. When you want the value *right now*\nfor one object — and are willing to pay for it on metered platforms — two\npass-through reads remain:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/accounts/ACCOUNT_ID/analytics -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/accounts/ACCOUNT_ID/media/MEDIA_ID/analytics -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\nThey return one object, no history and no comparison, and each one is billed on\nX. Prefer `/v1/analytics/*` for anything you'd put in a dashboard.\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"How collection works\" icon=\"rotate\" href=\"/concepts/analytics-collection\">\n    Cadences, freshness, history depth, and what each platform actually exposes.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Try it live\" icon=\"code\" href=\"/api-reference\">\n    Every analytics endpoint in the playground.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\n\n=================== guides/webhooks.md\n# Webhooks\n\n> Get told when a post goes live, a message arrives, or an account drops.\n\nRegister an HTTPS endpoint and PlugKit posts an event to it when something\nhappens — no polling.\n\n## Create an endpoint\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl -X POST https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"url\": \"https://your-app.com/hooks/plugkit\",\n    \"events\": [\"post.published\", \"message.received\"]\n  }'\n```\n\nOmit `events` (or send an empty list) to receive everything, including events\nadded later.\n\n<Warning>\n  The response contains the signing secret (`whsec_…`) **once**. Store it now —\n  it is never shown again, and you need it to verify deliveries.\n</Warning>\n\n## Events\n\n| Event | Fired when |\n| - | - |\n| `post.published` | The post is live on every one of its targets. |\n| `post.partial` | Some targets published, others failed. |\n| `post.failed` | No target published. |\n| `message.received` | An inbound message landed in the inbox. |\n| `comment.received` | A comment arrived on one of the account's posts. |\n| `comment.dm_sent` | A [comment → DM automation](/guides/campaigns) sent its private message. |\n| `broadcast.finished` | A broadcast finished serving every recipient. |\n| `account.disconnected` | An account was disconnected, or its token died. |\n| `usage.threshold_reached` | Pay-per-call spend passed 80% of the monthly cap — once a month, before anything pauses. |\n\nThe list is closed and names are `object.past_tense`. New events are added over\ntime; existing ones are never renamed.\n\n## Payload\n\nEvery delivery shares one envelope:\n\n```json theme={null}\n{\n  \"id\": \"evt_9f2c…\",\n  \"type\": \"post.published\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T14:31:02.184Z\",\n  \"data\": { }\n}\n```\n\n`data` carries the resource in the same shape the REST API returns it, so the\npost in `post.published` is the post you'd get from `GET /v1/posts/{id}`.\n\n## Verifying a delivery\n\nEach request carries an `x-plugkit-signature` header:\n\n```\nx-plugkit-signature: t=1756045862,v1=6f3b…\n```\n\n`v1` is the HMAC-SHA256 of `<t>.<raw body>`, keyed with your endpoint secret.\nCompute it over the **raw** body — parsing and re-serialising the JSON changes\nthe bytes and breaks the comparison.\n\n<CodeGroup>\n  ```ts TypeScript theme={null}\n  import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from \"crypto\";\n\n  function verify(rawBody: string, header: string, secret: string): boolean {\n    const parts = Object.fromEntries(\n      header.split(\",\").map((kv) => kv.split(\"=\") as [string, string]),\n    );\n    const expected = createHmac(\"sha256\", secret)\n      .update(`${parts.t}.${rawBody}`)\n      .digest(\"hex\");\n\n    // Reject anything older than five minutes to blunt replays.\n    if (Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number(parts.t)) > 300) return false;\n\n    return timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(expected), Buffer.from(parts.v1));\n  }\n  ```\n\n  ```python Python theme={null}\n  import hmac, hashlib, time\n\n  def verify(raw_body: bytes, header: str, secret: str) -> bool:\n      parts = dict(kv.split(\"=\", 1) for kv in header.split(\",\"))\n      expected = hmac.new(\n          secret.encode(), f\"{parts['t']}.\".encode() + raw_body, hashlib.sha256\n      ).hexdigest()\n      if abs(time.time() - int(parts[\"t\"])) > 300:\n          return False\n      return hmac.compare_digest(expected, parts[\"v1\"])\n  ```\n</CodeGroup>\n\n## Delivery and retries\n\nAnswer `2xx` within **10 seconds**. Anything else — an error status, a timeout,\na connection refused — is retried up to **6 attempts** with backoff: 30s, 2min,\n8min, 32min, \\~2h, then the delivery is marked `FAILED`.\n\nEvents are queued and sent by a worker, never inside the request that triggered\nthem. A slow endpoint of yours never slows down a publication, and a broken one\nnever makes it fail.\n\nDeliveries are **at least once**: a retry after a response you sent late will\narrive twice. Deduplicate on the payload's `id`.\n\nInspect what happened:\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID/deliveries \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\nEach row carries the event, the attempt count, the response status and the last\nerror.\n\n## Managing endpoints\n\n```bash theme={null}\ncurl https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n\ncurl -X PATCH https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{ \"enabled\": false }'\n\ncurl -X DELETE https://api.plugkit.co/v1/webhooks/WEBHOOK_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk_your_key\"\n```\n\n<Note>\n  These are PlugKit's **outbound** webhooks. The inbound plumbing — subscribing\n  an account to Meta's own webhooks so DMs reach the inbox at all — happens\n  automatically when an account is connected. It can be re-run for Instagram\n  (`POST /v1/connect/instagram/{accountId}/subscribe-webhooks`) and WhatsApp\n  (`POST /v1/connect/whatsapp/{accountId}/subscribe-webhooks`); a Facebook Page\n  subscribes once at connection time, so a Page that missed it has to be\n  reconnected.\n</Note>\n\n\n=================== mcp/overview.md\n# MCP server\n\n> Give Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, VS Code or any MCP client the ability to publish, read and reply on your social accounts.\n\nPlugKit ships a hosted **MCP server**: the same capabilities as the REST API,\nexposed as tools an AI assistant can call. Point a client at one URL, sign in,\nand the assistant can list your connected accounts, publish a post, triage the\ninbox, or pull analytics — no code, no SDK.\n\n```\nhttps://api.plugkit.co/mcp\n```\n\n<Note>\n  Transport is **Streamable HTTP** (stateless). There is nothing to install and\n  nothing to run locally — no `npx`, no local proxy.\n</Note>\n\n## Connect in one click\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"Claude\" icon=\"message\" href=\"/mcp/clients#claude-web-desktop-mobile\">\n    Customize → Connectors → Add → Custom connector → paste the URL.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"ChatGPT\" icon=\"sparkles\" href=\"/mcp/clients#chatgpt\">\n    Developer mode → chatgpt.com/plugins → **+** → paste the URL.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Claude Code\" icon=\"terminal\" href=\"/mcp/clients#claude-code\">\n    `claude mcp add -t http plugkit https://api.plugkit.co/mcp`\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Cursor\" icon=\"arrow-pointer\" href=\"/mcp/clients#cursor\">\n    One-click install link, or three lines in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"VS Code\" icon=\"code\" href=\"/mcp/clients#vs-code\">\n    One-click install link, or `code --add-mcp`.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\nFastest path of all: **[Assistants & API keys](https://plugkit.co/dashboard/mcp)**\nin the dashboard walks through one client at a time, with an install button or\nthe exact values to paste — and then confirms when the server has actually seen\nyour assistant connect.\n\n## Authentication\n\nTwo ways in, same account scoping as the REST API — an assistant only ever sees\nthe profiles, accounts, posts and conversations of the PlugKit user it acts for.\n\n<Tabs>\n  <Tab title=\"Sign in (OAuth)\">\n    The recommended path, and the only one that needs no secret in a config file.\n    PlugKit is a full OAuth 2.1 authorization server (PKCE, no client secret): the\n    client sends you to a PlugKit consent screen, you approve, and it stores a\n    token of its own.\n\n    You choose what you grant:\n\n    | Scope | What the assistant can do |\n    | - | - |\n    | `mcp:read` | Read profiles, accounts, posts, conversations and analytics. Write tools are not even listed. |\n    | `mcp:write` | Everything above, plus publish, send messages, reply to comments, connect and disconnect accounts. |\n\n    Revoke any assistant at any time from **Settings → Connected apps** in the\n    dashboard.\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"API key\">\n    For clients without OAuth support, send a key as a plain Bearer header:\n\n    ```json theme={null}\n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"plugkit\": {\n          \"type\": \"http\",\n          \"url\": \"https://api.plugkit.co/mcp\",\n          \"headers\": { \"Authorization\": \"Bearer sk_your_key\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n\n    Create the key in the dashboard's [API Keys](https://plugkit.co/dashboard/api-keys)\n    section. A key carries **full access** — it has no scopes — so prefer OAuth\n    when the client supports it.\n  </Tab>\n</Tabs>\n\n## What an assistant can do\n\n<CardGroup cols={2}>\n  <Card title=\"Publish\" icon=\"paper-plane\">\n    Draft, schedule and publish to several accounts at once, with media.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Inbox\" icon=\"inbox\">\n    Read and answer Instagram, WhatsApp and Telegram conversations.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Comments\" icon=\"comments\">\n    Read comments on a published post and reply publicly.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Analytics\" icon=\"chart-line\">\n    Ranked posts, trends, follower growth and best posting times — read from the\n    collected store, so one call covers every account.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Campaigns & ads\" icon=\"bullhorn\">\n    Comment → DM automations, broadcasts, follow-up sequences, and Meta ad\n    campaigns.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"Connections\" icon=\"plug\">\n    Hand the user an OAuth link to connect a new account, or disconnect one.\n  </Card>\n\n  <Card title=\"All 103 tools\" icon=\"wrench\" href=\"/mcp/tools\">\n    The full reference, plus the three ready-made workflows.\n  </Card>\n</CardGroup>\n\n## Safety\n\nPublishing a post, sending a message and replying to a comment are **public and\nimmediate**. The server instructs the model to show the exact content and get\nyour approval before calling those tools, but that is a prompt, not a lock — the\nreal guarantees are the ones you control:\n\n* Grant `mcp:read` only, when you just want reporting and triage.\n* Review the accounts a connected assistant can reach with `whoami`.\n* Revoke from **Settings → Connected apps** the moment you're done.\n\n<Warning>\n  `delete_profile` cascades to its accounts, posts and conversations, and\n  `revoke_api_key` can revoke the very key the connection runs on. Both are\n  write-scope tools — another reason to hand out `mcp:read` by default.\n</Warning>","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","interrupted":false